  "status": "PROVED EXACT CURRENCY CONVERSION",
  "task": "X56 h=2 anchored surplus currency",
  "theorem": "For each anchored nonzero h=2 source pair {1,a}, the number of disjoint target pairs is m_{1+a}-1.  X48 gives exactly 2*m_C ratios a with 1+a in a quotient coset C, so the anchored surplus is sum_C 2*m_C*(m_C-1) = 4*sum_C C(m_C,2).  X54 gives N_surplus = n*sum_C C(m_C,2), hence 4*N_surplus = n*A_anchor_surplus.  Therefore X55 is equivalent in anchored currency to A_anchor_surplus < 4*C(T(n)+1,2)."
